values ('a1b2c3d4-5e6f-4b21-8c01-1d2e3f4a5b11', 'biological-physical-anthropology', 'Biological / Physical Anthropology', 'Biological / Physical Anthropology introduces human evolution and biological diversity through evolutionary theory, genetics, primatology, skeletal anatomy, paleoanthropology, bioarchaeology, forensics, adaptation, and ethics. The course emphasizes scientific reasoning, multiple lines of evidence, anti-racist communication about human variation, and respectful work with human remains and descendant communities.');

